---
// Agents: the sidebar as the thing that tells you who needs you. The window is
// the real one from the canvas at 1:1; scripts/sections.ts runs a small loop
// on it while it is on screen: a session is working, goes still, asks for
// permission, and a notification comes in.
import Sidebar from '../../app/gen/Sidebar.astro';
import TerminalNarrow from '../../app/gen/TerminalNarrow.astro';
---
<section class="sec" id="coding-agents">
  <div class="page">
    <div class="bhead" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="h2">Know which agent needs you. <span class="tone">Hand one repository to Claude Code, another to Codex, a third to Aider. Wortel reads the screen and marks what is working and what is waiting.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="shot crop" style="--at: 18% 70%" data-agents aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="win wapp" inert>
        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-sidebar backdrop-blur-[50px] backdrop-saturate-[1.8]"></div>
        <div class="relative flex size-full">
          <div class="flex w-[234px] shrink-0"><Sidebar /></div>
          <div class="w-px shrink-0 bg-sidebar-border"></div>
          <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-1"><TerminalNarrow /></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="note" data-note>
        <img src="/icon-128.png" width="40" height="40" alt="" />
        <div class="txt">
          <p class="ttl"><b>Landing page hero</b><span>now</span></p>
          <p class="msg">Claude wants to run <span class="mono">npm run build</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ul class="facts" data-reveal-group>
      <li class="fact" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="h3">Working</h3>
        <p class="body">Output that keeps moving is an agent at work. Nothing is installed into the agent and nothing is written into its configuration.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="fact" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="h3">Waiting on you</h3>
        <p class="body">A screen gone still is a question, a permission or a stop. The session gets a dot, and a notification arrives if you were looking elsewhere.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="fact" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="h3">Next in line <kbd>⌥⇧⌘↓</kbd></h3>
        <p class="body">One key jumps to the next session that is waiting. Anything still running when you quit is picked back up on launch.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .note {
    position: absolute; z-index: 2; top: 24px; right: 24px; width: 344px;
    display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; padding: 12px 16px 12px 12px;
    border-radius: 18px;
    background: rgb(246 246 246 / 0.78);
    backdrop-filter: blur(24px) saturate(1.8); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(24px) saturate(1.8);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 0.5px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.12), 0 8px 24px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.14);
    font-family: var(--font-sans); color: #1d1d1f;
    opacity: 0; transform: translateX(380px);
  }
  .note img { width: 40px; height: 40px; flex: none; }
  .note p { margin: 0; }
  .txt { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
  .ttl { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 13px; line-height: 16px; }
  .ttl span { opacity: 0.5; font-size: 12px; }
  .msg { font-size: 13px; line-height: 16px; opacity: 0.8; }
  .msg .mono { font-size: 12px; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    .note { background: rgb(40 40 40 / 0.78); color: #f5f5f7; box-shadow: 0 0 0 0.5px rgb(255 255 255 / 0.14), 0 8px 24px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.4); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .note { right: 16px; top: 16px; width: 296px; } }
</style>
